+ * SCHED_WRR: a weighted round-robin scheduling class.
+ *
+ * CSPB 3753 scheduler assignment -- STARTER CODE.
+ *
+ * Every CPU has a FIFO queue of runnable SCHED_WRR tasks (rq->wrr.queue).
+ * The task at the head of the queue runs. A task of weight w may run for
+ * WRR_TIMESLICE(w) ticks (w * 10 ms); when that slice is used up the task
+ * moves to the tail and the next task gets its turn. When every task on a
+ * CPU is CPU-bound, a task's share of that CPU is w / (sum of weights).
+ *
+ * The class sits between RT and CFS: stop > deadline > rt > wrr > fair > idle
+ * (see SCHED_DATA in include/asm-generic/vmlinux.lds.h).
+ *
+ * Data structures (already declared for you):
+ *   struct sched_wrr_entity   p->wrr       include/linux/sched.h
+ *   struct wrr_rq             rq->wrr      kernel/sched/sched.h
